            <ArticleTitle>Shotgun Sphingolipid Analysis of Human Aqueous Humor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-107</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/978-1-4939-7407-8_10</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This protocol provides a step-by-step guide to shotgun sphingolipid analysis of aqueous humor. We describe the Bligh and Dyer crude lipid extraction method and electrospray ionization tandem mass spectrometry (ESI-MS/MS) coupled with MZmine 2.21 data processing for identification and ratiometric quantitation of sphingosine, sphingosine-1-phosphate, sphingomyelin, and ceramide.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
